---
import SaidLayout from "../../../layouts/SaidLayout.astro";
---

<SaidLayout
  title="Said and Done. is downloading — Windows"
  description="Your setup.exe is on its way. Per-user install, no admin prompt — just tell SmartScreen: More info, Run anyway."
>
  <section class="said-frame" style="padding-top: 48px;">
    <div class="said-wrap said-reveal">
      <p class="said-kicker">Downloading for Windows</p>
      <h2>Run it, tell SmartScreen it's fine<span class="dot">.</span></h2>
      <p>
        Your <code>setup.exe</code> is on its way. It installs per-user — no
        admin prompt, a normal Add/Remove entry, updates that can actually
        update.
      </p>

      <div class="said-after-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 240" role="img">
          <rect x="90" y="20" width="380" height="200" rx="14" fill="var(--said-card)" stroke="var(--said-line)" />
          <rect x="90" y="20" width="380" height="42" rx="14" fill="rgb(15 168 240 / 10%)" />
          <text x="114" y="47" font-family="var(--said-body)" font-size="13" fill="var(--said-ink)">Windows protected your PC</text>
          <text x="114" y="96" font-family="var(--said-body)" font-size="12" fill="var(--said-faint)">Microsoft Defender SmartScreen hasn't met</text>
          <text x="114" y="114" font-family="var(--said-body)" font-size="12" fill="var(--said-faint)">this app yet. That changes at release.</text>
          <text x="114" y="146" font-family="var(--said-body)" font-size="12" fill="var(--said-blue)" text-decoration="underline">More info</text>
          <rect x="304" y="168" width="140" height="34" rx="8" fill="rgb(15 168 240 / 22%)" stroke="var(--said-blue)" />
          <text x="374" y="190" font-family="var(--said-body)" font-size="13" fill="var(--said-ink)" text-anchor="middle">Run anyway</text>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <ol class="said-after-steps">
        <li>Run the downloaded <code>setup.exe</code>.</li>
        <li>SmartScreen may step in: click <strong>More info → Run anyway</strong>. Signing lands before release; until then Windows plays it safe.</li>
        <li>It installs to your user profile and appears in Start and Add/Remove like anything else.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="said-note said-after-note">
        No elevation means the self-updater can swap the app without asking an
        admin — updates that can actually update.
      </p>
      <div class="said-cta-row" style="margin-top: 26px;">
        <a class="said-btn said-btn-primary" href="/said-and-done/guides/first-boot/">First boot, step by step</a>
        <a class="said-btn said-btn-ghost" href="/said-and-done/download/">Back to downloads</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SaidLayout>
